  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "### 1(b) Decision tree on the whole data set\n\nThis is a multi-label problem: each patient has two binary labels. I used the **label powerset** method, combining the two labels into a single class: `00` = neither, `10` = inflammation only, `01` = nephritis only, `11` = both.\n\n**Is label powerset the right choice here?** Yes. The two diagnoses co-occur (19 of 120 patients have both), so the labels are not independent. Binary relevance would build one tree per label and ignore that dependence, while a label powerset tree learns the combinations directly. With only 4 possible combinations, all of which appear in the data, label powerset creates no sparse classes.",
   "id": "e31d3443"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "15611920",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "10    40\n",
      "01    31\n",
      "00    30\n",
      "11    19\n",
      "Name: count, dtype: int64\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1600x900 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier, plot_tree\n",
    "\n",
    "X_acute = acute[[\"temp\", \"nausea\", \"lumbar_pain\", \"urine_pushing\",\n",
    "                 \"micturition_pains\", \"burning_urethra\"]]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Label powerset: combine the two diagnoses into one label\n",
    "# \"00\" = neither, \"10\" = inflammation only, \"01\" = nephritis only, \"11\" = both\n",
    "y_acute = acute[\"inflammation\"].astype(str) + acute[\"nephritis\"].astype(str)\n",
    "print(y_acute.value_counts())\n",
    "\n",
    "tree = DecisionTreeClassifier(random_state=0)\n",
    "tree.fit(X_acute, y_acute)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(16, 9))\n",
    "plot_tree(tree, feature_names=X_acute.columns, class_names=tree.classes_,\n",
    "          filled=True, fontsize=9)\n",
    "plt.title(\"Decision tree on the full Acute Inflammations data (label powerset)\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "### 1(c) IF-THEN rules\n\nEach root-to-leaf path is one rule:",
   "id": "bd3ea9d9"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2dd6cba2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "IF lumbar_pain <= 0.50 AND temp <= 38.95  THEN class = 10   (n = 40)\n",
      "IF lumbar_pain <= 0.50 AND temp > 38.95  THEN class = 00   (n = 10)\n",
      "IF lumbar_pain > 0.50 AND temp <= 37.95  THEN class = 00   (n = 20)\n",
      "IF lumbar_pain > 0.50 AND temp > 37.95 AND micturition_pains <= 0.50  THEN class = 01   (n = 21)\n",
      "IF lumbar_pain > 0.50 AND temp > 37.95 AND micturition_pains > 0.50 AND urine_pushing <= 0.50  THEN class = 01   (n = 10)\n",
      "IF lumbar_pain > 0.50 AND temp > 37.95 AND micturition_pains > 0.50 AND urine_pushing > 0.50  THEN class = 11   (n = 19)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def tree_to_rules(model, feature_names):\n",
    "    t = model.tree_\n",
    "    rules = []\n",
    "    def walk(node, conds):\n",
    "        if t.children_left[node] == -1:  # leaf\n",
    "            cls = model.classes_[t.value[node][0].argmax()]\n",
    "            rules.append(\"IF \" + \" AND \".join(conds) +\n",
    "                         f\"  THEN class = {cls}   (n = {t.n_node_samples[node]})\")\n",
    "            return\n",
    "        name, thr = feature_names[t.feature[node]], t.threshold[node]\n",
    "        walk(t.children_left[node],  conds + [f\"{name} <= {thr:.2f}\"])\n",
    "        walk(t.children_right[node], conds + [f\"{name} > {thr:.2f}\"])\n",
    "    walk(0, [])\n",
    "    return rules\n",
    "\n",
    "for r in tree_to_rules(tree, list(X_acute.columns)):\n",
    "    print(r)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "In plain language (the symptom features are 0/1, so \"\u2264 0.5\" means *no* and \"> 0.5\" means *yes*):\n\n1. IF **no lumbar pain** AND **temperature \u2264 38.95** THEN **inflammation only** (40 patients)\n2. IF **no lumbar pain** AND **temperature > 38.95** THEN **neither disease** (10)\n3. IF **lumbar pain** AND **temperature \u2264 37.95** THEN **neither disease** (20)\n4. IF **lumbar pain** AND **temperature > 37.95** AND **no micturition pains** THEN **nephritis only** (21)\n5. IF **lumbar pain** AND **temperature > 37.95** AND **micturition pains** AND **no urine pushing** THEN **nephritis only** (10)\n6. IF **lumbar pain** AND **temperature > 37.95** AND **micturition pains** AND **urine pushing** THEN **both diseases** (19)\n\nEvery leaf is pure, so the tree classifies all 120 patients correctly. Nausea and burning of the urethra are never used.",
   "id": "2b8551c1"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
