   "source": "The heatmap shows several blocks of strongly correlated features (dark red), for example groups of income, poverty, and family-structure variables, and the count variables that scale with population size. There are also strong negative correlations (blue) between related variables, such as measures of affluence vs. poverty. This multicollinearity makes least-squares coefficients unstable and motivates ridge, LASSO, and PCR.",
