   "source": "| | Test MSE | Variables selected |\n|---|---|---|\n| LASSO (raw features) | 0.01768 | 77 of 122 |\n| LASSO (standardized features) | 0.01773 | 76 of 122 |\n\nThe two versions are nearly identical. The features are already normalized to [0, 1], so standardizing changes their relative scales only slightly, and the L1 penalty treats them almost the same way. Both models drop about 45 features, which is LASSO's built-in variable selection.",
   "id": "a0036e5a"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "#### 2(i) Principal components regression (M chosen by cross-validation)",
   "id": "cb213217"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "pcr_scores = []\nfor M in range(1, X_train.shape[1] + 1):\n    pcr = Pipeline([(\"pca\", PCA(n_components=M)), (\"lr\", LinearRegression())])\n    mse = -cross_val_score(pcr, X_train, y_train, cv=kf,\n                           scoring=\"neg_mean_squared_error\").mean()\n    pcr_scores.append((M, mse))\n\npcr_df = pd.DataFrame(pcr_scores, columns=[\"M\", \"cv_mse\"])\nbest_M = int(pcr_df.loc[pcr_df[\"cv_mse\"].idxmin(), \"M\"])\n\npcr = Pipeline([(\"pca\", PCA(n_components=best_M)), (\"lr\", LinearRegression())]).fit(X_train, y_train)\nresults[\"PCR\"] = mean_squared_error(y_test, pcr.predict(X_test))\nprint(\"Best M:\", best_M, \" Test MSE:\", results[\"PCR\"])\n\nplt.plot(pcr_df[\"M\"], pcr_df[\"cv_mse\"])\nplt.axvline(best_M, color=\"red\", linestyle=\"--\")\nplt.xlabel(\"Number of components M\"); plt.ylabel(\"CV MSE\"); plt.title(\"PCR: choosing M\")\nplt.show()",
   "id": "748e2c9e"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "#### 2(j) L1-penalized gradient boosting (XGBoost)\n\nXGBoost's `reg_alpha` is an L1 penalty on the leaf weights of the boosted trees; it is chosen by 5-fold cross-validation. Requires `pip install xgboost`.",
   "id": "77afe6e7"
