   "source": "The L1-penalized XGBoost model has the lowest test MSE (0.0161, with \u03b1 = 0.1 chosen by CV), about 8% lower than the best linear model. Boosted trees can capture non-linear effects and interactions that the linear models cannot. Among the linear models, ridge (\u03bb \u2248 2.31) performs best, followed closely by the two LASSO versions; least squares is the worst, as expected with 122 correlated features and no penalty. The differences among the linear models are small, so regularization helps only modestly here. See the PCR row for how dimension reduction compares.",
